{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Momentum: The model consistently fails to capture the magnitude of upward price spikes (e.g., the jump from ~85 to ~95+), forecasting only a slow, linear drift. Apply a positive bias correction of +5 to +10 EUR when the 3-day price momentum exceeds 3%.",
    "Sentiment Lag Correction: Positive sentiment signals (values > 0.20) are ignored by the model's linear projection. When sentiment history shows a value of 0.20 or higher, immediately adjust the forecast upward by 2-4 EUR to account for the delayed market reaction.",
    "Overshoot Correction on Volatility: The model assumes mean reversion to a flat trend, missing the volatility clustering where prices overshoot peaks before correcting. Reduce the forecast slope by 50% during the first 5 days of a confirmed breakout to prevent underestimating the peak, then apply a steeper mean-reversion decay in the subsequent 10 days.",
    "Horizon-Specific Bias: The error grows non-linearly with the forecast horizon. For horizons beyond 10 days, the model's linear extrapolation is insufficient; switch to a regime-switching logic that projects higher volatility bands rather than a single deterministic path.",
    "Reversion Speed Adjustment: The model is too slow to react to the sharp drop after the peak (e.g., from 100 down to 92). Increase the mean reversion speed parameter by 30% when the price exceeds the 20-day moving average by more than 15%."
  ]
}
